apy|v|To incline; to set at an angle; to tilt over; to tip upon the edge; as, to cant a cask; to cant a ship. ; To give a sudden turn or new direction to; as, to cant round a stick of timber; to cant a football. ; To cut off an angle from, as from a square piece of timber, or from the head of a bolt. ; To speak in a whining voice, or an affected, singsong tone. ; To make whining pretensions to goodness; to talk with an affectation of religion, philanthropy, etc.; to practice hypocrisy; as, a canting fanatic. ; To use pretentious language, barbarous jargon, or technical terms; to talk with an affectation of learning. ; to sell by auction, or bid a price at a sale by auction.	d:14yr,19,4~14yr,19,4
apy|a|Of the nature of cant; affected; vulgar.	j:sft,28,3;1upi,5,1;vdp,2,1~sft,28,3;vdp,2,1;1upi,5,1	e:14yr,14,3~14yr,14,3
