bad|n|One of the hereditary classes into which the Hindoos are divided according to the laws of Brahmanism. ; A separate and fixed order or class of persons in society who chiefly hold intercourse among themselves.	a:ymm,77,6~ymm,77,6
bas|n|of Cast ; The act of one who casts or throws, as in fishing. ; The act or process of making casts or impressions, or of shaping metal or plaster in a mold; the act or the process of pouring molten metal into a mold. ; That which is cast in a mold; esp. the mass of metal so cast; as, a casting in iron; bronze casting. ; The warping of a board. ; The act of casting off, or that which is cast off, as skin, feathers, excrement, etc.	a:2a4r,90,4~2a4r,90,4	v:1kfs,22,2~1kfs,22,2	n:13vj,91,5;2a4r,70,1;1a7p,31,1;1kfs,12,1~13vj,91,5;2a4r,70,1;1a7p,31,1;1kfs,12,1	N:1rb8,45,3;19bs,22,2~1rb8,45,3;19bs,22,2
